# Temporary "coming soon" gate. Every URL on the domain serves the
# coming-soon content while keeping its own address bar URL (status 200 =
# rewrite, not a redirect) — so worthkeeping.info shows it directly, not
# worthkeeping.info/coming-soon.
#
# The destination is a flat top-level file (coming-soon.html), not a
# folder. A folder (e.g. /coming-soon/, backed by index.html) is subject to
# Cloudflare's own directory<->index.html canonicalization, and any rule
# that points at it — in either form — gets flagged by Wrangler's deploy-time
# loop detector as feeding back into itself. A flat file has no such
# ambiguity, so it's immune to that check. This matches Cloudflare's own
# documented maintenance-mode pattern (/* /maintenance.html 200).
#
# These specific-path rules must stay above the catch-all: Cloudflare
# evaluates rules top-to-bottom and stops at the first match, so anything
# the coming-soon page itself loads (its own CSS/JS/images) needs to be
# excluded here or it would get swept into the rewrite too and come back
# as HTML instead of CSS/JS/images.

/styles.css              /styles.css               200
/script.js               /script.js                200
/robots.txt              /robots.txt               200
/sitemap.xml             /sitemap.xml              200
/assets/*                /assets/:splat            200

/*                       /coming-soon.html          200
